{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0427","billNumberShort":"H.B. 427","billNumberLong":"HB0427","fileNumber":"2026FL0312","shortTitle":"Tax Increment Financing Modifications","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"WALTER","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Walter, R. Neil","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies the process by which a public entity may utilize tax increment financing.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>beginning July 1, 2026, requires a public entity seeking to utilize tax increment to first:<hr><ltbullet1>conduct an application authorization meeting; and<hr><ltbullet1>submit an application to the Governor's Office of Economic Opportunity (office); <hr><ltbullet>authorizes the office to review an application and:<hr><ltbullet1>approve the application; or<hr><ltbullet1>if the information in the application is unclear, vague, or demonstrably inaccurate, deny the application;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes a public entity that receives an approved application to begin the process to trigger and utilize tax increment;<hr><ltbullet>requires a public entity that receives more revenue from tax increment than anticipated to utilize the revenue to defease bonds or otherwise accelerate repayment of debt incurred by the public entity; and<hr><ltbullet>requires the office to ensure certain information from an application is made publicly available.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"RuthAnne Oakey-Frost","fiscalAnalyst":"Josh Pittman","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"IGOOQSXTFT","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 08:26:26.477","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHo